<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:0}h2{font-size:15px;margin:0 0 8px}
p{margin:0 0 10px}ul{margin:0 0 10px 18px;padding:0}code{font:12px Menlo,monospace}</style>
</head><body>
<h2>Geant4 @VERSION@</h2>
<p>This installs Geant4 @VERSION@ into <code>@PREFIX@</code>.</p>
<p>The data files are <b>not</b> in this package. The next page lets you choose
which ones you want, and they are downloaded from
<code>cern.ch/geant4-data</code> while the installation runs, so the machine
needs to be online at that point. Each download is checked against the MD5
that <code>geant4-config</code> records before it is unpacked.</p>
<p>All twelve datasets are selected. Seven of them are required: Geant4 turns
their absence into a fatal error the moment it builds its physics tables. The
other five are needed only for specific physics (neutron transport with the
<code>_hp</code> physics lists, PIXE, optical surfaces, the SAID cross-sections
and crystal channelling) and account for about 1.3 GB of the 1.65 GB download.
Untick any you do not need.</p>
<p>A dataset left out can be added later without reinstalling, for example:</p>
<p><code>sudo @PREFIX@/share/Geant4/fetch-datasets.sh --only G4NDL</code></p>
</body></html>
